The Monkey is a horror, comedy film directed by Osgood Perkins.

3
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:16,000
When twin brothers find a mysterious wind-up monkey, a series
of outrageous deaths tear their family apart.

4
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:39,333
Twenty-five years later, the monkey begins a new killing spree
forcing the estranged brothers to confront the cursed toy.

5
00:26:56,666 --> 00:27:02,666
Hal / Bill, played by Theo James.

6
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Lois, played by Tatiana Maslany.

7
00:37:43,333 --> 00:37:49,333
Young Hal / Young Bill, played by Christian Convery.

8
00:43:06,666 --> 00:43:12,666
Petey, played by Colin O'Brien.

9
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Captain Petey Shelborn, played by Adam Scott.

10
00:53:53,333 --> 00:53:59,333
Ted, played by Elijah Wood.

11
00:59:16,666 --> 00:59:22,666
The Monkey is a 2025 American comedy horror film
written and directed by Osgood Perkins.

12
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
Based on Stephen King's 1980 short story, the film stars Theo James in a dual role as twin brothers whose lives
are turned upside down by a cursed toy monkey that causes random horrific deaths around them.

13
01:10:03,333 --> 01:10:09,333
Tatiana Maslany, Christian Convery, Colin O'Brien, Rohan Campbell,
Sarah Levy, Adam Scott, and Elijah Wood also star.

14
01:15:26,666 --> 01:15:32,666
The Monkey was theatrically released in the United
States by Neon on February 21, 2025.

15
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:56,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and has grossed
$68.9 million worldwide against a budget of $10–11 million.

16
01:26:13,333 --> 01:26:19,333
The film explores themes of sibling relationship,
shotgun, supernatural, drums, harpoon.

17
01:31:36,666 --> 01:31:42,666
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
